WEBVTT

00:14:28.458 --> 00:14:32.476
So we've each become
a little bit more like the other.

00:14:32.500 --> 00:14:34.167
So what did you learn about trust?

00:14:35.583 --> 00:14:37.351
EP: This was really interesting,

00:14:37.375 --> 00:14:40.601
because -- I mean,
I can say a lot of things

00:14:40.625 --> 00:14:42.434
as how I think about trust.

00:14:42.458 --> 00:14:44.268
But when I went to look at research,

00:14:44.292 --> 00:14:48.059
what it fundamentally said is that
there is an absolute definitional void.

00:14:48.083 --> 00:14:52.143
It is one of those concepts
that is swimming in vagueness.

00:14:52.167 --> 00:14:55.018
There is a view that reinforces the notion

00:14:55.042 --> 00:14:57.809
that trust is a psychological state

00:14:57.833 --> 00:15:01.601
in which you express
the willingness to be vulnerable,